Well... I did once have that idea. It never got anywhere, mainly because
of three reasons:
- my Inform knowledge is not nearly up to the task yet;
- I wasn't sure whether the NetHack license would be compatible with the
IF Comp's requirements;
- when all is said and done, it would have been a mildly amusing
in-joke, nothing more. You'd have to either ditch too much, and lose all
the nit-picky balancing acts that make NetHack so much fun; or present
the IF player with so much detail that it'd be impossible to slog
through using the command structure of a text adventure; or worst of
all, try and find the golden middle road and end up suffering from both
failures. I couldn't find a good way to avoid this. If you can, well,
I'm putting this one on a back-burner, and I won't be too annoyed if you
beat me to it.

